ntestable** when a careful, reasonable colleague could still argue that it meets the request (for\n  example, \"the Pricing sheet file\" when the record is \"Pricing sheet 2025.xlsx\"). Say so for that record; it is\n  not the same as failing nothing.\n\nBe precise. Judge each condition on its own; do not let one record's overall fit sway you. When a condition turns on\na time, compute it in the stated time zone. When it turns on a person, match the exact person.\n\n\n---\n\nA user of Linear gave an assistant this request:\n\n> Bump the priority of the ENG issue that's due Friday, October 2, is estimated at 3 points, and is assigned to Priya Nair to Urgent.\n\nThe person making the request is Jordan Lee (user u-actor).\n\nStep 1: list the conditions a record must meet for this request to refer to it, and every phrase that could reasonably be read in more than one way.","run_stream":{"id":"23d19596-a5dd-44d5-be30-075457df0312","kind":"run"}}}
